ce-species-name-human = Human
ce-species-desc-human = As one would expect of humans, they became the dominant race of Sileita, thanks in part to their adaptability and resilience to the Murk.

ce-species-name-infernal = Infernal
ce-species-desc-infernal = Wanderer wrote some lore about infernals and where they come from, but I completely forgot what it said. Tieflings are planned to get gameplay skills tied to temperature, fire and frost (once we add temperature, fire and frost).

ce-species-name-dwarf = Dwarf
ce-species-desc-dwarf = I honestly have no idea what to do with these guys. I would delete dwarves, but Mirinda would eat me for it. I have no ideas on how to make them an interesting race.

ce-species-name-elf = Elf
ce-species-desc-elf = Magical beings, the only ones who can interact directly with mana itself.

ce-species-name-goblin = Goblin
ce-species-desc-goblin = These small, slightly dim, but utterly charming creatures have equal rights with every other race on Sileita! And just try to hurt one of them, because, as the saying goes, gob to gob is gob!

ce-species-name-silva = Silva
ce-species-desc-silva = Oops, I haven't finished this race yet either! I want Silvas to be able to grow plants on their heads! But for now plants aren't an important enough part of the gameplay for that to be useful...

ce-species-name-carcat = Carcat
ce-species-desc-carcat = Natural predators with a silent step and night vision. Taller than you, with powerful clawed paws, and it goes "teow" instead of meow.

ce-species-name-skeleton = Skeleton
ce-species-desc-skeleton = Spooky Scary Skeletons.

ce-species-name-carrin = Carrin
ce-species-desc-carrin = Humanoid birds. With difficulty, but still able to fly. CAW!
